 "dependency_review": "Inspected the intake row (notion_id 3b431704-6eeb-816e-b743-fe9d0892b0c8, recording 2026-09-21 14-33-14, topic 'GPT Luna is now free for Free and Go users of ChatGPT, and GPT 5.6 Sol is on the desktop app'), the approved plan (lane 'icon choreography'), scene handoff and whiteboard notes, and the TITLE constant of the approved split generator ('GPT Luna is free in ChatGPT'), which all three index.html titles carry and is the package title; the Notion idea ID is the short_id. The three editable projects each carry index.html; every local src/href resolves inside its tree, and the whiteboard's assets folder is a symlink into stage/lunafree_whiteboard that delivery materializes as real files. Generators: lunafree_scene.py, the split, cutout (plus envelope) and whiteboard generators and _lunafree_proof.py; their imports resolve to pipeline/captions.py, pipeline/pointing_cues.py, formats/cutout/lib (cutout_core, cutout_depthfield) and formats/whiteboard/lib (whiteboard_build, whiteboard_fix6_core), all included; the rest is stdlib, numpy and PIL. Media and timing: the raw recording, its full Scribe transcript, the whole cuts/lunafree set (master, face plates, audio, EDL, tight transcript) and the seven prep stage records. Matting: the matting/lunafree session (selection and chair-carve edits, v5 alpha/cut/rim layers with pre-fallback copies, plates, prompts, headroom, fallback fb1 records, ship record) and the matting_fallback/lunafree session. Config and paperwork: every gen/_*lunafree* build, BiRefNet master, cue, envelope, gate, geometry, prerender, pill-width, QC, render-control, spec and whiteboard record. Review: final_lunafree.json (Miguel's approval on the staged videos), agent start/done/state records, the Astra matte prompt, log and result, matte reviews including the rejected fb1 anatomy set, proof crops, sheets and the legacy phone records; the Astra pid file is excluded as runtime state. External runtime dependencies recorded, not vend